			But spare me the political statement nonsense. Every tool becomes a lifestyle brand to make people feel superior. PTA isn't a revolution—it's a boring, reliable choice, and that's exactly why it'll outlive the next ten 'disruptive' accounting startups. Show me the prod deployment of your double-entry ledger that's been running since 2003 without a database migration. That's a real achievement, not a manifesto.

			So yeah, plain text is cool, the same way a hammer is cool. It doesn't need a TED talk. It just needs to not break when you hit your thumb. Which is more than I can say for whatever 'intelligent' accounting SaaS is burning VC money this quarter to reinvent the CSV file.
